<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Derivation for Reverse Update Decomposition</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this part, we formally derive the DPS algorithm with DDIM sampling to our gradient perspective decomposition <a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3.1. Reverse Update Decomposition ‣ 3. A Gradient Perspective on Reverse Process ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The standard DDIM sampling with <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}=0</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{\prime}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\left(\frac{\mathbf{x}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{\prime}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\left(\frac{\mathbf{x}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\prod_{s=1}^{t}\alpha_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\prod_{s=1}^{t}\alpha_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cumulative product of the noise schedule, and <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the estimated noise obtained from the learned network.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Rewriting the scaling term,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">we express <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}-\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}-\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}-\left(\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}-\left(\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}-\left(\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}-\left(\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Here, the second term represents the denoising gradient, which we denote as:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}_{d}(\mathbf{x}_{t})=\left(\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}_{d}(\mathbf{x}_{t})=\left(\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For conditional generation based on measurement <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, DPS introduce an additional likelihood update:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t-1}=\mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{\prime}-\zeta\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\|\mathbf{y}-\mathcal{A}(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t}))\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t-1}=\mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{\prime}-\zeta\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\|\mathbf{y}-\mathcal{A}(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t}))\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the observed data, <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is the observation operator, and <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the estimated clean image given by:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t})=\frac{\mathbf{x}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t})=\frac{\mathbf{x}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">The likelihood gradient term is thus defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t})=\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\|\mathbf{y}-\mathcal{A}(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t}))\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t})=\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\|\mathbf{y}-\mathcal{A}(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t}))\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, the complete algorithm in an gradient perspective can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E21X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t-1}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t-1}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}}_{\text{fixed scaling}}-\underbrace{\left(\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{{\alpha}_{t}}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\bm{\epsilon}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)}_{\text{denoising gradient}~\mathbf{g}_{d}(\mathbf{x}_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>fixed scaling</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>denoising gradient</mtext><mo lspace="0.270em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}}_{\text{fixed scaling}}-\underbrace{\left(\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{{\alpha}_{t}}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\bm{\epsilon}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{t},t)}_{\text{denoising gradient}~\mathbf{g}_{d}(\mathbf{x}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E21Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-{\zeta}\underbrace{\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\|\mathbf{y}-\mathcal{A}(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t}))\|_{2}^{2}}_{\text{likelihood gradient}~\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>likelihood gradient</mtext><mo lspace="0.270em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-{\zeta}\underbrace{\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}}\|\mathbf{y}-\mathcal{A}(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{0}(\mathbf{x}_{t}))\|_{2}^{2}}_{\text{likelihood gradient}~\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E21Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}}_{\text{fixed scaling}}-\underbrace{\mathbf{g}_{d}(\mathbf{x}_{t})}_{\text{denoising gradient}}-\zeta\underbrace{\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t})}_{\text{likelihood gradient}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>fixed scaling</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>denoising gradient</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>likelihood gradient</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\mathbf{x}_{t}}_{\text{fixed scaling}}-\underbrace{\mathbf{g}_{d}(\mathbf{x}_{t})}_{\text{denoising gradient}}-\zeta\underbrace{\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t})}_{\text{likelihood gradient}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">which matches the <a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3.1. Reverse Update Decomposition ‣ 3. A Gradient Perspective on Reverse Process ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> in the main paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1. </span>Descent Lemma for L-Smooth Functions</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To support the proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1. ‣ 4.3. Theoretical Analysis ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we first state and prove the following lemma concerning functions with <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth gradients.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_theorem">Lemma B.1.</h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a continuously differentiable function whose gradient <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz continuous for some <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-\nabla f(\mathbf{w})\|_{2}\leq L\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-\nabla f(\mathbf{w})\|_{2}\leq L\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w},\mathbf{w}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w},\mathbf{w}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w},\mathbf{w}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w},\mathbf{w}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})\leq f(\mathbf{w})+\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})\leq f(\mathbf{w})+\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus for vector functions, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-f(\mathbf{w})=\int_{0}^{1}\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w})),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-f(\mathbf{w})=\int_{0}^{1}\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w})),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Adding and subtracting <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle=\int_{0}^{1}\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle=\int_{0}^{1}\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-f(\mathbf{w})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-f(\mathbf{w})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+\int_{0}^{1}\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+\int_{0}^{1}\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality to the integrand:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))-\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))-\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))-\nabla f(\mathbf{w})\|_{2}\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))-\nabla f(\mathbf{w})\|_{2}\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using the <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz property of the gradient <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))-\nabla f(\mathbf{w})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla f(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))-\nabla f(\mathbf{w})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L\|(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L\|(\mathbf{w}+t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}))-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L\|t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L\|t(\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Lt\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Lt\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this back into the integral bound:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-f(\mathbf{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-f(\mathbf{w})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+\int_{0}^{1}(Lt\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2})\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+\int_{0}^{1}(Lt\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2})\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+L\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}^{2}\int_{0}^{1}t\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+L\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}^{2}\int_{0}^{1}t\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Evaluating the integral <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}t\,dt=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}t\,dt=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-f(\mathbf{w})\leq\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\mathbf{w}^{\prime})-f(\mathbf{w})\leq\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{w}),\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">which gives the desired inequality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2. </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1. ‣ 4.3. Theoretical Analysis ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1. ‣ 4.3. Theoretical Analysis ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We apply the Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1. Descent Lemma for L-Smooth Functions ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> to each iteration <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> of the SPGD warm-up loop (Line 9 in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.1. Progressive Warm-Up Phase ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, with <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math>). The update is <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)}=\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)}-\eta\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)}=\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)}-\eta\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=L_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}=\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}=\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}^{\prime}=\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}^{\prime}=\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The displacement is <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}=-\eta\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}^{\prime}-\mathbf{w}=-\eta\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{w})</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting into Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1. Descent Lemma for L-Smooth Functions ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})+\langle\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)}),-\eta\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|-\eta\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})+\langle\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)}),-\eta\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|-\eta\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})-\eta\langle\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)}),\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\eta^{2}\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})-\eta\langle\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)}),\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\eta^{2}\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})-\eta\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})-\eta\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})-\eta\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})-\eta\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">The condition <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&lt;1/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&lt;1/L</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-L\eta/2)&gt;1/2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-L\eta/2)&gt;1/2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, each warm-up step guarantees a non-increasing likelihood objective, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})\leq L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})\leq L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})</annotation></semantics></math>, with strict decrease if <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\neq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\neq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Summing this per-step inequality over <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0,\dots,N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0,\dots,N-1</annotation></semantics></math> yields:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(30)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})]\leq\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\left[-\eta\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})]\leq\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\left[-\eta\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The right-hand side can be simplified by moving the constant factors outside the summation:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})]\leq-\eta\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})]\leq-\eta\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The left-hand side of Eq. (<a href="#A2.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Proof of . ‣ B.2. Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) is a telescoping sum:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j+1)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(1)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(0)})]+[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(2)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(1)})]+\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(1)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(0)})]+[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(2)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(1)})]+\dots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dots+[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N-1)})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dots+[L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N-1)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this back, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(0)})\leq-\eta\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})-L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(0)})\leq-\eta\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging this inequality to isolate <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})</annotation></semantics></math> yields the final result stated in the proposition:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})\leq L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(0)})-\eta\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(N)})\leq L_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(0)})-\eta\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\left(1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\right)\|\mathbf{g}_{l}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{(j)})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>More Discussions</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1. </span>Novel Aspects of SPGD</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While prior works have explored momentum-based techniques <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chung et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and multi-step likelihood updates <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, SPGD’s novelty lies in three key areas:</p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Analysis-Driven Motivation:</span> Our core contribution is the novel gradient-centric analysis identifying the dual problems of <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">gradient conflict</span> and <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">gradient fluctuation</span>. SPGD’s components are not an ad-hoc combination but are directly motivated by this analysis to solve these specific, identified issues, providing a principled foundation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Technical Novelty of ADM:</span> Unlike prior works that use standard, constant momentum, our ADM is technically more advanced. It dynamically adjusts the momentum strength based on directional consistency (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 4.2. Momentum-Based Likelihood Gradient Smoothing ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>)), making it more robust than a fixed momentum coefficient, as validated in our ablation studies.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Synergistic Design:</span> Our warm-up phase is specifically designed to mitigate gradient conflict before the denoising step. This creates a stable context that enables ADM to effectively dampen fluctuations. The synergistic combination of a conflict-mitigating warm-up with a fluctuation-dampening ADM is a unique design absent in prior art.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F7.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="132.59" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429 132.59" width="429"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,132.59) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-0.28,0) translate(0,-0.28)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.28 0.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31em;--ltx-fo-height:8.31em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="115" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 115)" width="429.01"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2507.06656v1/figs/components.jpg" id="A3.F7.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/115;" width="429" height="115" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.34 116.53)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="47.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1" class="ltx_text">baseline</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 101.29 117.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.99em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="55.16"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2" class="ltx_text">w/ ADM</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 177.28 117.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="75.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.3" class="ltx_text">w/ warm-up</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 278.47 116.58)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="44.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0073BD;">SPGD</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 359.84 116.53)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.87em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="53.5"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.5" class="ltx_text">reference</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>. </span><span id="A3.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Visual results of ablation study on design components. The complete SPGD shows clearer hair textures.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2. </span>Relation to Pixel-as-Parameter (PxP)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our SPGD method shares conceptual ground with Pixel-as-Parameter (PxP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dinh et al., 2023</a>)</cite> in viewing the reverse process through a gradient lens and acknowledging potential gradient conflicts. However, our solutions are fundamentally different.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">PxP’s approach is to explicitly <span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">resolve</span> conflicts by projecting gradients to enforce orthogonality before the update. In contrast, SPGD aims to <span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">mitigate</span> conflicts by using a progressive warm-up phase. This phase allows the state <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to gradually adapt to the likelihood guidance <span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">before</span> the denoising step is applied. We adopt this strategy because we found that explicit gradient projection can lead to information loss and degrade performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, PxP computes all guidance terms from the initial <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and applies them in a single, combined update. SPGD’s architecture is different, introducing an inner loop that iteratively refines <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with the likelihood gradient prior to denoising. In essence, SPGD employs sequential refinement for conflict mitigation, whereas PxP uses simultaneous projection for conflict resolution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3. </span>ADM Stability</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While a full theoretical convergence proof for SPGD with ADM is a significant undertaking beyond the scope of this paper, we can provide further intuition on its stability. The ADM update rule, <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{g}}_{l}^{(j)}=\alpha_{j}\beta\widetilde{\mathbf{g}}_{l}^{(j-1)}+(1-\alpha_{j}\beta)\mathbf{g}_{l}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{g}}_{l}^{(j)}=\alpha_{j}\beta\widetilde{\mathbf{g}}_{l}^{(j-1)}+(1-\alpha_{j}\beta)\mathbf{g}_{l}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, can be interpreted as a standard momentum update with a dynamically adjusted momentum coefficient <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}=\alpha_{j}\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}=\alpha_{j}\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The stability of standard momentum methods is well-understood and often relies on the step size and momentum coefficient being within certain bounds related to the properties of the objective function (e.g., its smoothness <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and strong convexity <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>). Our adaptive weight <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that the effective momentum <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is always less than or equal to the base coefficient <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math>). When the gradient direction changes abruptly, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> decreases, reducing the effective momentum <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. This reduction pushes the update behavior closer to that of standard gradient descent, a method with well-known and robust convergence guarantees under standard assumptions (e.g., sufficiently small step size).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In essence, ADM acts as a self-stabilizing mechanism. It leverages the acceleration benefits of momentum when the optimization landscape is smooth and consistent, but reduces its reliance on momentum precisely when the gradient signal becomes noisy or changes direction sharply. This connection to the more conservative gradient descent method provides strong theoretical intuition for why ADM contributes to the overall stability of the SPGD framework.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1. </span>Comparison Methods</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure a fair comparison, all pixel-based diffusion methods (Score-SDE, MCG, DDRM, DPS, DiffPIR, DPPS, and RED-Diff) share the same pre-trained checkpoint. Below, we describe our implementation details for each method.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PnP-ADMM:</span> We use the pre-trained DnCNN model from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2017</a>)</cite>. The regularization parameter is set to <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>, and the algorithm is run for 10 iterations on all tasks.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Score-SDE:</span> In Score-SDE, data consistency is enforced via a projection step following unconditional diffusion denoising at every iteration. The projection configuration follows the recommendations in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chung et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MCG:</span> Our implementation of MCG is based on the source code provided in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chung et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. We replicate the evaluation settings reported in the paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DPS:</span> Experimental outcomes for DPS are obtained from the implementation in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chung et al., 2023</a>)</cite> using 1,000 DDPM sampling steps. All hyper-parameters are set as suggested in D.1 section of the corresponding paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DDRM:</span> For DDRM, we utilize 20 NFEs DDIM sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2021a</a>)</cite> with parameters <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0.85</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{B}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{B}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, as recommended in the literature.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DiffPIR:</span> We adopt the original code of DiffPIR from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. We adjust the diffusion steps to 20 for implementation efficiency. Hyper-parameters are selected to reflect the settings for the noiseless case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DPPS:</span> We follow the default configuration as provided by the open-sourced code in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RED-Diff:</span> The implementation for RED-Diff is adopted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mardani et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. We use the Adam optimizer over 1,000 steps, setting <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.25</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lr=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lr=0.25</annotation></semantics></math>, consistent with the experimental settings in the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2. </span>Our SPGD:</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For our SPGD implementation detailed in <a href="#alg1" title="In 4.1. Progressive Warm-Up Phase ‣ 4. Proposed Method ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we follow the time step discretization and noise schedule from EDM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. We use <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=100</annotation></semantics></math> outer diffusion steps. Each outer step includes <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=5</annotation></semantics></math> inner warm-up iterations, corresponding to 500 NFEs in total. The base momentum coefficient for ADM is set to <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The learning rate <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned separately for each task. The specific values are provided in <a href="#A4.T5" title="In D.2. Our SPGD: ‣ Appendix D Implementation Details ‣ Enhancing Diffusion Model Stability for Image Restorationvia Gradient Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>. </span><span id="A4.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Learning rates <math id="A4.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> for each task.</span></figcaption>
